# TODO app

Run from this Cargo project:

```sh
cargo run -- help
cargo run -- add "Buy milk"
cargo run -- list
cargo run -- complete 1
cargo run -- delete 1
```

Each invocation performs one command. `add` takes exactly one description
argument: quote spaces, use `""` for an empty description, and quote a leading
hyphen normally (`add "-urgent"`). `complete` and `delete` take one unsigned
decimal `u64` ID. `list` and `help` take no operands. No arguments, `-h`, and
`--help` also show help. List rows are `ID [ ] description` for incomplete tasks
and `ID [x] description` for completed tasks; an empty list prints `No tasks.`
Add, complete and delete confirmations identify the affected ID.

Successful commands exit 0 and write stdout. Operation/storage failures exit 1;
usage failures exit 2. Failures write stderr and leave stdout empty. Help and
usage failures do not access storage. Storage is `tasks.json` in the build-time
Cargo project root, independent of the invocation working directory.

